ated to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=cos⁡\\theta ,\\,y=sin⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=\\frac{7}{8}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $sin⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{7}{8})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{49}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we select the positive answer since $sin⁡\\theta $ is positive in the first quadrant. So our final answer is $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["4a5d9b12-19cd-584b-b779-a468e4d6ca2a"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "8e1ea995-d6ac-507a-b61c-f3087c637df3" :answer/id #uuid "8e1ea995-d6ac-507a-b61c-f3087c637df3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fd2e1cc1-cb15-5e19-b2ed-06cfc90ef286" :answer/id #uuid "fd2e1cc1-cb15-5e19-b2ed-06cfc90ef286" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8dc4b2b4-ef85-5136-ae4f-475a2d6e7ccc" :answer/id #uuid "8dc4b2b4-ef85-5136-ae4f-475a2d6e7ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5524e754-213c-5297-b6c8-38ca120bb015" :answer/id #uuid "5524e754-213c-5297-b6c8-38ca120bb015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "037cbbc0-15eb-5ca5-9687-929e9c03c3b6" :answer/id #uuid "037cbbc0-15eb-5ca5-9687-929e9c03c3b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1aa6be0a-2bd9-5771-ae42-ec